# L §8.2 `unknown day:` (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P9, Q4): a hole inside a record's field or a tuple's
# item carries its unknown day as a whole result's hole does: `unknown day: w` under each. Before: no line.
=== m.tally
model rec
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2019-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source card "invented"
input w: date
input d0: date
input n1: int
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2019-01-01
  w = window(2024-02-27, 2024-03-02) "c"
  d0 = 2024-02-28 "c"
  n1 = 1 "c"
ask in_record: (a: w < d0, b: n1)
ask in_tuple: w < d0, n1
ask rec_month: (a: month_of(w), b: n1)
ask list_month: [w, d0]
=== expect
in_record: (a: ?"date within window(2024-02-27, 2024-03-02) not precise enough for w < d0" (w), b: 1)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
in_tuple: (?"date within window(2024-02-27, 2024-03-02) not precise enough for w < d0" (w), 1)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
list_month: [window(2024-02-27, 2024-03-02), 2024-02-28]
  cut 2026-01-01
rec_month: (a: ?"date within window(2024-02-27, 2024-03-02) not precise enough for month_of" (w), b: 1)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
